                        <![CDATA[Unitree might be the world’s most important robotics company.]]>
                    </description>
                                                                <content:encoded>
                            <![CDATA[<p>On a sunny morning in June, I walked to work with a quadruped robot beside me. I’ve never gotten more attention from strangers.</p>
<p>A bunch of people snapped pictures of my robot dog. Several people asked me questions. Was it mine? (Yes.) Did I build it? (No.) Was it being used for surveillance? (No.)</p>
<p>Biological dogs kept a safe distance from my mechanical companion. Some growled or barked at it.</p><p><a href="https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2026/09/i-spent-4000-on-a-robot-dog-from-china/">Read full article</a></p>
